{
  "schema_version": "fabric.resume-token-vectors/v2",
  "rule": "Spec 050 §3.6: a resume token is 'fr3/' + the run correlation id + '/' + a predecessor entry (<segment_id>/<source_id>/<epoch>/<last_sequence>/sha256:<manifest digest>), optionally '/br-<32 hex>'. The correlation id is the root segment's run id: r- + 32 hex (the mapped clear id, or minted when the caller gave none); in clear mode (explicit opt-in, R8) a caller-rooted run's clear id as given (or its h- form), which then crosses the boundary in baggage. It matches ^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:-]{0,127}$ (no '/'), else the token is not issued (api_misuse). 'fr2/' tokens (no correlation id) are parsed for one release. A malformed token is dropped (tokens_rejected). Run identity at segment open, first rule that applies: 1 one correlation id among valid fr3 tokens -> it, verbatim (token); 2 differing ids and a clear run id -> the mapped clear id (caller_join); 3 differing ids, no run id -> the lowest by byte order (token_conflict); 4 no valid fr3 token and a clear run id (argument or same-host FABRIC_RUN_ID) -> the mapped clear id (caller); 5 neither -> a minted r- + 32 CSPRNG hex (minted). Rules 4 and 5 report legacy when the only valid tokens are fr2. Mapping (identity rule): pseudonymous mode maps every caller value whatever its shape (r- + 32 hex of HMAC-SHA256(key, value), SHA-256 without a key); only an EmittedId of the handle passes through; clear mode emits it as given (h- + 40 hex of SHA-256 when it is not an opaque id). minted stands in for the CSPRNG draw. end_run refuses without a valid token, and with run_id None and tokens of different runs.",
